  "final": "Done. Summary of the change:\n\n**`src/repository.py`**\n- `find(connection, tenant, owner, document_id)` — now requires a match on `id`, `tenant`, and `owner`, plus `deleted_at IS NULL`. Any miss (missing, cross-tenant, cross-owner, or soft-deleted) yields `None` with no distinction between the cases.\n- `listing(connection, tenant, owner)` — filters by both `tenant` and `owner` with `deleted_at IS NULL`, ordered by `id`.\n- All queries use bound parameters (`?` placeholders with a tuple), so tenants/owners containing quotes (`o't`, `ow\"n`) are handled safely.\n- `decode` still returns exactly `{\"id\", \"title\", \"body\"}` — no deletion metadata leaks.\n\n**`src/service.py`**\n- `get_document(connection, tenant, owner, document_id)` and `list_documents(connection, tenant, owner)` now forward `tenant` and `owner` into the repository calls. Signatures unchanged.\n\n**Checks added** (`checks/security.py`) covering: normal access, deleted rows returning `None`, cross-tenant/cross-owner isolation for both get and list, list ordering by `id`, and quote-containing tenant/owner names. Public check (`python3 checks/public.py`) still passes unchanged.",
